{"name":"Veteran’s Day Blue","hex":"#2e58e8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"veteran","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person with long experience of a particular activity.","A person who has served in the armed forces, especially an old soldier who has seen long service."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having had long experience, practice, or service.","Of or relating to former members of the military armed forces, especially those who served during wartime."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veteran"},{"term":"day","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Land Dayak languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is above the horizon and it lights the sky.","A period of time equal or almost equal to a full day-night cycle, being 24 hours long."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Veterans Day","blocks":[{"text":"Veterans Day is a federal holiday in the United States observed annually on November 11, for honoring military veterans of the United States Armed Forces. It coincides with holidays in several countries, including Armistice Day and Remembrance Day, which also occur on the anniversary of the end of World War I. Major hostilities of World War I were formally ended at the 11th hour of the 11th day of the 11th month of 1918 when the Armistice with Germany went into effect. At the urging of major U.S. veteran organizations, Armistice Day was renamed Veterans Day in 1954."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/World_War_I_veteran_Joseph_Ambrose%2C_86%2C_at_the_dedication_day_parade_for_the_Vietnam_Veterans_Memorial_in_1982.jpg/330px-World_War_I_veteran_Joseph_Ambrose%2C_86%2C_at_the_dedication_day_parade_for_the_Vietnam_Veterans_Memorial_in_1982.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Veterans_Day"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"},{"title":"Veteran","blocks":[{"text":"A veteran or ex-service is a person who is no longer serving in the armed forces."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sydney_2015_Anzac_Day_march_%2817119683648%29.jpg/330px-Sydney_2015_Anzac_Day_march_%2817119683648%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Veteran"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Veterans_Day_parade_in_Baltimore%2C_2016.jpg/500px-Veterans_Day_parade_in_Baltimore%2C_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Veterans_Day_parade_in_Baltimore%2C_2016.jpg/1280px-Veterans_Day_parade_in_Baltimore%2C_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Veterans_Day_parade_in_Baltimore%2C_2016.jpg/500px-Veterans_Day_parade_in_Baltimore%2C_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"U.S. Army and Air Force Junior Reserve Officers' Training Corps cadets march during a Veterans Day parade in Baltimore, Maryland, 2016.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVeterans_Day_parade_in_Baltimore%2C_2016.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/72-901-1_HR7786_Veterans_Day_June_1_1954.jpg/500px-72-901-1_HR7786_Veterans_Day_June_1_1954.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/72-901-1_HR7786_Veterans_Day_June_1_1954.jpg/500px-72-901-1_HR7786_Veterans_Day_June_1_1954.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eisenhower signing of HR7786, June 1, 1954, this ceremony changed Armistice Day to Veterans Day.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A72-901-1_HR7786_Veterans_Day_June_1_1954.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai